-- Worldforged pickups (maps 750 / 751): pickups take CoA's height where DC kept the stock terrain (CoA 8623c9cc4).
-- Until now a CoA height within 3 yd of the terrain was snapped onto DC's terrain, and one more than 3 yd above it was
-- snapped down unless a DC spawn stood at that height. That was right while CoA's heights were rough. Since then CoA
-- snapped its floating pickups to the stock terrain (rev_20261006_65), restored the ones that stand on buildings, and
-- checked hundreds in game and in the world editor. A CoA height still above the terrain is a floor, a table, a crate
-- or a tower: barn floors (#10835), the Fenris Keep floor, a mausoleum (#10974), Shaul'watha (#11362). Where DC's
-- terrain is identical to stock (within 0.1 yd) those buildings are the same, so the pickup now stands on them instead
-- of on the ground beneath, often inside or under the model. Where DC changed the terrain, or CoA's height is below
-- it, nothing changes.
-- - 123 pickups move up, Z only (0.3 to 18.7 yd); no x/y, zone or item changes.
-- - 3 pickups that had no trustworthy height are added: a Fishing Box, an Old Crate and a Tiki Shield floating on the
--   water at the heights Ascension's client recorded (like the Floating Barrel), with one new item clone each.
-- No spawn guid changes, so every character keeps its claims.
